# SizeKit — Engineering

## Before coding

1. Inspect existing code; reuse components/utilities.
2. Read Expo SDK 57 docs (`https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/`) before Expo APIs.
3. Smallest clean change; no unrelated rewrites.
4. Ask before major architecture decisions; proceed on small obvious details.

## UI / code

- Minimal deps; no large UI frameworks without clear need
- Reusable components; focused screens (no monoliths)
- Simple nav; don't over-engineer early
- User-facing errors must be plain language (never raw exceptions)
- Guard memory: large/4K images, cleanup, avoid loading multiple full-res bitmaps

## Dependencies

Before installing: needed? Expo already provides it? Maintained? SDK 57 compatible? Native complexity? Recurring cost? Prefer fewer packages.

## Security

Never commit secrets, keys, tokens, or signing material. Only claim "files stay on device" when true.

## Do not auto-add

Analytics, ads SDKs, or billing SDKs without discussion. When adding ads/Pro later, keep them behind service abstractions.

## Git

Clear, focused commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`). No giant unrelated commits. Only commit when the user asks.
